# Contractor missions

When asked to build a specification end-to-end, run it as a **mission** rather
than editing files directly.

**Nothing is built until a validation contract exists and a human has approved
it.** The contract defines "done" independently of the implementation.

## Load the prompt for the phase you are in

```bash
contractor prompt mission     # the loop and the standing rules
contractor prompt plan        # phase 1 — contract + milestones, then BLOCK for approval
contractor prompt run         # phase 2 — build
contractor prompt validate    # phase 3 — adjudicate
```

Seat prompts: `contractor prompt seats/worker` · `seats/validator` ·
`seats/escalation-worker` · `seats/reviewer` · `seats/simplifier`.

## Before starting

```bash
contractor doctor
```

Errors mean the harness is not adapted to this repository yet. Run
`contractor prompt init`, follow it, re-run `doctor`.

## Seats in Cursor

Cursor has no subagent primitive, so **you provide the context boundary**:

- Keep the **orchestrator** in one chat for the whole mission.
- Open a **new chat per worker**, pasting only that seat's prompt and payload.
- Open a **new chat per validator**, and give it no history from the worker's
  chat. That freshness is the entire mechanism — a validator that saw the
  implementation is not a verifier.

Do not run a validator in the same chat that wrote the code. It will agree with
itself, and the verdict is worthless.

## Never re-derive these — the CLI decides

```bash
contractor partition <milestone>   # which features may run in parallel
contractor escalate <files…>       # inline or delegate, and the worker's grant
contractor advance                 # advance / corrective / circuit-break
contractor check                   # bookkeeping invariants
contractor brief                   # the rehydration digest, for a fresh chat
contractor own <paths…>            # which area owns a path
```

## Boundaries

A worker edits **only** its area's `pathGlobs`. Anything else is an escalation:
record it with the exact file list and stop. Run `contractor own <path>` when
unsure.

## Finish

```bash
contractor disarm <halted|gated|done> <missionDir>
contractor status     # must print INERT
```

**`gated` is not `done`.** Any assertion that could not be verified in-harness
bars `done` and becomes a follow-up with its exact commands.
